From: PowOS <noreply@powback.com>
Subject: [PATCH] desktop containment: widgets keep their size while the desktop is narrower

On a phone the desktop narrows often - split screen, a floating window - and AppletsLayout relaid the widgets out
for each new width: every one shrunk to fit (down to its minimum), and that saved over the real layout (the
horizontal / vertical fallback too), so they stayed broken afterwards. The relayout is locked while the desktop is
narrower than the widest it has been this session: widgets keep their size and place, nothing is saved, and back
at that width AppletsLayout restores the saved layout exactly.
---
--- a/containments/desktop/package/contents/ui/main.qml
+++ b/containments/desktop/package/contents/ui/main.qml
@@ -288,7 +288,19 @@
         ContainmentLayoutManager.AppletsLayout {
             id: appletsLayout
             anchors.fill: parent
+            // PowOS: and while the desktop is narrower than it has been (split screen or a floating window on a
+            // phone): widgets keep their size and place - the relayout shrank every one to fit, and saved that over
+            // the real layout - until it is back to the width they were laid out at, which restores it exactly.
             relayoutLock: width !== root.availableScreenRect.width || height !== root.availableScreenRect.height
+                || root.availableScreenRect.width < widestWidth
+            property real widestWidth: 0
+            Connections {
+                target: root
+                function onAvailableScreenRectChanged() {
+                    appletsLayout.widestWidth = Math.max(appletsLayout.widestWidth, root.availableScreenRect.width);
+                }
+            }
+            Component.onCompleted: widestWidth = Math.max(widestWidth, root.availableScreenRect.width)
             // NOTE: use root.availableScreenRect and not own width and height as they are updated not atomically
             configKey: "ItemGeometries-" + Math.round(root.screenGeometry.width) + "x" + Math.round(root.screenGeometry.height)
             fallbackConfigKey: root.availableScreenRect.width > root.availableScreenRect.height ? "ItemGeometriesHorizontal" : "ItemGeometriesVertical"
